@startuml
title Sequence Diagram 02 - Virtual Waiting Room Flow

actor "Customer" as Customer
participant "Web / Mobile Client" as Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Waiting Room Service" as WaitingRoom
database "Redis Queue" as Redis
participant "Event Catalog Service" as Catalog

Customer -> Client: Open high-demand event page
Client -> Gateway: Request event access
Gateway -> WaitingRoom: Check traffic and queue status

alt Traffic is normal
    WaitingRoom --> Gateway: Access allowed
    Gateway -> Catalog: Load event details
    Catalog --> Gateway: Event details
    Gateway --> Client: Show event page
else Traffic is high
    WaitingRoom -> Redis: Add user to waiting queue
    Redis --> WaitingRoom: Queue position saved
    WaitingRoom --> Gateway: Return queue position
    Gateway --> Client: Show waiting room page
    Client --> Customer: Display queue position

    loop Until user turn arrives
        Client -> Gateway: Poll queue status
        Gateway -> WaitingRoom: Check user position
        WaitingRoom -> Redis: Read queue position
        Redis --> WaitingRoom: Current position
        WaitingRoom --> Gateway: Queue status
        Gateway --> Client: Update waiting position
    end

    WaitingRoom -> Redis: Mark user as allowed
    WaitingRoom --> Gateway: Access allowed
    Gateway -> Catalog: Load event details
    Catalog --> Gateway: Event details
    Gateway --> Client: Show event page
end

@enduml
